rows.body:
Primary intended execution environment: GEX44.

Before assuming any setup:

Reality Scan the current GEX44 state.

Determine:

current user/account;

current Claude Code/runtime version;

existing Claude Power Pack checkout or clone;

active branches/worktrees;

existing missions/workers;

resource state;

available CPU/RAM/storage;

GEX44-specific capabilities;

current toolchain/runtime state;

existing KSR/KME/reconstruction artifacts;

current mission ownership.

Do not create a duplicate CPP clone, duplicate mission, duplicate daemon or competing owner if the necessary state already exists.

Use the current canonical source of truth.

If some mutation must occur elsewhere because repository reality requires it, Claude Code decides that from evidence while GEX44 remains the primary mission execution environment where appropriate.

Before substantial architecture mutation:

perform Reality Scan;

reconstruct current ownership;

read the required institutional sources;

inspect current implementation;

inspect current tests/benchmarks;

inspect recent relevant commits;

inspect active missions/workers;

compile the master Work Graph;

compile the initial economic model;

then present ONE inline master plan in chat for one-click Owner approval.

The plan must NOT be replaced by a standalone plan file.

It may additionally be backed up to the current canonical plan mechanism.

The Owner should be able to approve the whole mission with one response.

After that approval:

continue autonomously.

Do not return for approval at each wave.

Do not return for normal token-budget drift.

Do not return for ordinary refactors.

Do not return for implementation choices.

Only use Human Decision Firewall for genuine authority boundaries.

The inline plan MUST contain a serious bottom-up token budget before the Owner approves execution.

This is mandatory.

Do not estimate cost by:

number of phases × historical phase cost;

number of plans × historical plan cost;

arbitrary token allowance;

“similar missions usually cost X” alone.

Compile the budget from the actual current Work Graph.

First define the accounting unit explicitly.

Prefer processed tokens or the current canonical Cognitive Economy unit if the repository has superseded it.

State exactly what the unit includes.

Never leave the unit ambiguous.

For the complete mission provide:

measured historical baseline where available;

current starting floor;

low estimate;

central estimate;

high estimate;

expected model-bound calls;

expected average context per call or equivalent working-set estimate;

expected deterministic/zero-model share;

expected Sonnet share;

expected stronger/frontier-model share;

expected Agent Team cost;

expected verification/proof cost;

expected benchmark/replay cost;

expected architecture CAPEX;

expected implementation OPEX;

expected contingency;

estimated wall-clock;

expected GEX44 compute;

expected external/hardware dependencies if any.

Also provide a token-budget breakdown for every major Work Stream or proof wave.

The plan must distinguish:

ONE-TIME CAPEX

Reusable infrastructure being built.

MISSION OPEX

Cost necessary to execute/prove this mission.

ASSURANCE COST

Independent verification, mutation, red-team and Production Reality.

CONTINGENCY

Real uncertainty, not arbitrary padding.

The plan must show:

Budget before self-hosting improvements.

Expected budget after the mission starts consuming its own certified optimizations.

Expected savings attributable to each major self-hosted capability where evidence permits.

The budget must therefore be dynamic.

The programme is expected to become cheaper while executing if its architecture is working.

The Owner requested that the plan expose token budget.

The Owner also requested that the mission continue until complete.

Therefore:

do not turn the forecast into a repeated permission gate unless the Owner explicitly supplies a hard cap.

After initial approval:

budget drift triggers automatic ECONOMIC RECOMPILE, not an Owner interruption.

If actual spend materially diverges from forecast:

pause the affected execution lane;

determine the causal source;

recalculate remaining Work Graph;

identify whether the mission is suffering:

context rent;

extra model boundaries;

proof amplification;

agent duplication;

unexpected novelty;

incorrect scope;

architecture regression;

tool failure;

new required work;

or bad original estimation;

improve the factory where ROI warrants it;

continue.

If provider quota physically prevents execution, persist mission state and WAIT without losing the Goal.

Do not fabricate execution beyond external resource reality.

Use:

C:\Users\User\Downloads\Promptsss\Prompts pa iterar\Universal\iteracion-avanzada-universal.txt

as a mandatory iteration input.

Apply it:

after Reality Scan before presenting the inline plan;

when architecture materially changes;

before final red-team/completion.

The iteration file does not outrank:

Owner intent;

current repository reality;

CLAUDE.md;

UKDL;

verified evidence;

Production Reality.

Do not let iteration become architecture inflation.

This prompt contains ZERO implementation code.

That is intentional.

Treat adding implementation code into this mission constitution as a kill-switch violation.

The prompt defines:

mission;

outcomes;

laws;

contracts;

evidence requirements;

authority;

completion criteria.

Claude Code decides implementation from repository reality.

Do not mechanically create files/classes/services based on names used here.

Names are conceptual unless an existing owner already uses them.

Do not create another:

GSD runtime;

Mission OS;

Memory OS;

Context OS;

Cognitive OS;

Knowledge DB;

Capability Registry;

Agent Registry;

Git manager;

scheduler;

proof system;

Baseline Ratchet;

Maturity Engine;

Graph store;

Reconstruction OS;

Autonomous Optimization OS;

permanent daemon;

long-horizon controller

if current CPP already has the responsible owner.

This mission should make existing architecture denser and more capable.

Not wider and more duplicated.

The North Star is not tokens.

The North Star is:

MINIMUM TOTAL VERIFIED COST TO REQUIRED REALITY

with correctness, evidence strength, authority and Production Reality as hard constraints.

Cost includes where relevant:

model tokens;

context traffic;

model boundaries;

tool calls;

CPU;

RAM;

compile time;

GEX44;

Dolphin;

hardware;

calendar latency;

proof;

repair;

human attention;

maintenance burden;

risk.

Value includes:

verified product progress;

uncertainty removed;

critical-path closure;

future work eliminated;

knowledge created;

capabilities created;

failure recurrence prevented;

future cost avoided.

NO COGNITIVE COST IS ACCEPTABLE MERELY BECAUSE IT FITS WITHIN BUDGET.

EVERY MATERIAL COST MUST PURCHASE AT LEAST ONE OF:

verified progress;

verified assurance;

verified new information;

verified future cost reduction.

During EVERY GSD X session the runtime should be capable, with low overhead, of noticing opportunities to improve the engineering process itself.

It should autonomously discover patterns such as:

repeated computation;

repeated raw scans;

repeated unchanged reads;

repeated reasoning;

repeated plans;

repeated proof;

repeated builds;

repeated environment setup;

repeated runtime experiments;

duplicate agents;

model-driven polling;

dead context;

stale context;

tool-output carriage;

high scan amplification;

high read amplification;

high proof amplification;

high reasoning amplification;

high model-boundary amplification;

large context for tiny decisions;

large source closure for local change;

frequent human interruptions that can be eliminated;

lack of observability causing repeated archaeology;

deterministic work still routed through models;

hot paths that should become compiled operations;

failure classes repeatedly diagnosed manually;

infrastructure used rarely enough to retire.

This capability must not rely solely on Claude remembering to look for opportunities.

Compile detection into telemetry/runtime where feasible.

The current Opportunity Delegation Principle must stop being only prompt doctrine.

Compile it into the architecture.

The system should be able to generate a durable Optimization Candidate containing enough semantics to answer:

what repeated cost exists;

what evidence proves it;

how often it occurs;

what projects/workloads pay it;

whether it affects the critical path;

what the current owner is;

whether a current capability already solves it;

what transformation might remove it;

what implementation CAPEX it requires;

what verification cost it requires;

what maintenance tax it adds;

what expected current-mission saving exists;

what expected future-estate saving exists;

what risk exists;

what scope it should have;

how it will be benchmarked;

when it should be retired.

Use existing data structures if capable.

Do not create unnecessary parallel state.

Use KME-L as a canonical initial real-world optimization incident.

The reported symptom is that KME-L may scan the broad ~/.claude/projects estate and therefore touch large amounts of session history across unrelated repos, including CostaLuz, to answer KME-focused analytical questions.

Do NOT assume that description is still exact.

Reality-scan it.

Measure:

what paths it scans;

what objects are unique;

what junctions/symlinks alias existing data;

how many sessions exist;

how many belong to KME;

how many are mixed-workstream sessions;

unique bytes;

duplicate bytes;

previously processed bytes;

raw bytes read per query;

derived evidence actually consumed;

which metrics are recomputed;

which query shapes recur;

which indexes already exist;

which FIOS/usage-index/CVM/CIF capabilities already cover the problem;

cross-project raw-evidence exposure;

parser/instrument validity;

freshness semantics.

Then allow the Autonomous Optimization capability to discover the opportunity structurally.

Do not hard-code:

IF KME-L THEN OPTIMIZE SCANNING.

The system must recognize the general smell:

LOCAL QUESTION + GLOBAL IMMUTABLE CORPUS + REPEATED SCAN + TINY RELEVANT SUBSET + STABLE DERIVATIONS.

Where KME-L reality confirms the problem, evolve normal analysis toward:

raw evidence ingested once per valid identity/version;

canonical deduplication;

structured events/derived state;

project/workstream attribution;

queryable indexes;

incremental aggregates;

dependency-aware derivations;

materialized views for recurring queries;

progressive aperture;

raw evidence only on demand.

Normal analytical cost should approach:

delta + query-relevant dependency closure.

Not:

entire historical estate.

Raw transcripts remain authoritative cold evidence.

They cease being the normal operational database.

KME-L is not sufficient proof.

After solving the real KME-L hotspot, identify at least one structurally analogous burden elsewhere without the Owner naming it.

Examples may include:

test-result rescanning;

source rereads;

proof repetition;

build repetition;

planning subagent amplification;

tool output carriage;

context rent;

query recomputation;

duplicate corpus processing;

repeated deterministic model calls.

Choose from reality.

Prove the opportunity miner learned a pattern, not a KME-L special case.

Build/extend the Reconstruction Factory as the universal institutional capability for reconstructing software or behavior from arbitrary reference evidence.

It must support different reference classes without pretending every domain is identical.

Potential references include:

source fragments;

binary;

assembly;

runtime behavior;

screenshots;

images;

video;

logs;

assets;

network traces;

APIs;

live systems;

hardware;

emulators;

documents;

multiple references jointly.

The universal kernel should reason about:

identity;

state;

evidence;

uncertainty;

contracts;

dependencies;

causality;

equivalence;

proof;

intervention;

cost.

Domain adapters own domain semantics.

KSR's approximately 34k-function corpus must never automatically become approximately 34k LLM tasks.

A function count is physical inventory.

Not cognitive inventory.

The factory must first search for latent structure:

exact donors;

normalized donors;

cross-title homologues;

libraries;

SDK/runtime;

compiler-generated regions;

templates;

families;

types;

classes;

vtables;

object/TU structure;

state-machine structure;

data-layout structure;

shared engine logic;

sport-specific logic;

known behavioral interfaces;

opaque reusable regions;

novel semantic residual.

The expensive frontier is the residual.

Allow the architecture to distinguish levels such as, if repository reality supports them:

opaque but contract-proven;

binary-owned;

structurally understood;

semantically understood;

behaviorally understood/equivalent;

source-owned;

byte-equivalent.

Do not pay maximum reconstruction depth for every component.

Compile the minimum depth required by the actual product/proof contract.

FULL archaeology and product-critical intervention may have different closure frontiers.

Before execution, compile a human Goal into an executable semantic plan.

Do not execute a giant prompt as the runtime.

Use or extend existing Mission/Goal IR.

The compiled mission should expose, where useful:

desired state;

current state;

open semantic delta;

proof obligations;

unknowns;

dependencies;

reusable capabilities;

existing evidence;

possible execution strategies;

model boundaries;

resource needs;

side-effect boundaries;

completion contract.

Then run compiler-like optimization passes against that representation.

Evaluate, reuse or implement only where evidence supports them:

already-satisfied elimination;

Proof of Non-Work;

dead-work elimination;

common-work elimination;

duplicate derivation elimination;

baseline inheritance;

capability specialization;

partial evaluation;

constant/applicability folding;

known-family substitution;

cross-title reuse;

proof reuse;

observation reuse;

build reuse;

semantic-cache reuse;

work-unit fusion;

work-unit fission;

batching;

parallelization;

context working-set compilation;

deterministic transaction compilation;

model-boundary placement;

critical-path optimization;

speculative preparation;

deoptimization guards.

The purpose is to make execution cheaper before it starts.

A required outcome may have several valid strategies.

Examples:

reuse;

known transform;

source reconstruction;

family solver;

compiler search;

runtime experiment;

semantic adapter;

retail relink;

existing proof;

behavioral reconstruction;

frontier reasoning.

Represent alternatives through the current architecture rather than one hard-coded planning grammar.

Choose the lowest Expected Total Verified Cost route that satisfies:

authority;

correctness;

proof;

Production Reality.

Treat model cognition as one resource among many.

The scheduler/allocator should reason about:

model quota;

model quality;

context;

CPU;

RAM;

compiler lanes;

Dolphin/runtime lanes;

GEX44 availability;

hardware availability;

wall clock;

verification;

human attention;

risk.

A more expensive model may be economically correct when it removes a critical blocker with huge downstream leverage.

A cheap model is wasteful when it repeatedly handles a deterministic operation.

Do not assume a fixed price for resources.

Their opportunity cost depends on reality.

Examples:

idle compiler capacity may be cheap;

busy GEX44 critical lane may be expensive;

Owner physical Wii availability may be scarce;

frontier quota may need reservation for novel blockers;

a hardware boot may dominate calendar cost;

a deterministic CPU batch may be essentially free relative to cognition.

Use current evidence.

Do not construct fake financial precision.

Distinguish:

COGNITIVE OPEX

Reasoning that resolves one instance and disappears.

COGNITIVE CAPEX

Reasoning/engineering that creates reusable:

family solver;

compiler rule;

type model;

index;

oracle;

detector;

proof recipe;

benchmark;

context compiler;

failure immunity;

automation;

capability.

Frontier cognition that creates large reusable capital can be economically excellent.

Repeated OPEX on a known class is debt.

For material new factory capabilities estimate:

build cost;

verification cost;

maintenance cost;

expected uses;

current cost/use;

future cost/use;

expected lifetime saving;

transfer scope;

risk;

time-to-payback.

Do not build infrastructure because it sounds sophisticated.

Build when expected amortization dominates.

If later realized dividend is poor:

narrow or retire.

Detect when a repeated decision still requires model cognition despite enough evidence existing to automate/compile it.

That is Reasoning Debt.

Examples:

same mismatch manually classified dozens of times;

same architecture fact rediscovered;

same source family repeatedly reasoned;

same next-step orchestration decision made by models;

same proof interpreted manually.

Reasoning Debt becomes an Optimization Candidate.

The desired lifecycle of repeated cognition is:

reasoned once;

remembered;

recognized as repeated;

structured;

converted into decision procedure;

converted into solver/tool;

compiled into baseline;

decision disappears.

Maturity should be visible as fewer decisions requiring models.

Every model call should be attributable to a semantic reason.

Use existing taxonomy if one exists.

Useful concepts include:

NOVELTY;

AMBIGUITY;

AUTHORITY;

STATE_MISS;

CAPABILITY_MISS;

CONTEXT_FAULT;

TOOLING_MISS;

OBSERVABILITY_MISS;

PROOF_FAULT;

RECOVERY_MISS;

CONTROL_LOOP_MISS;

DISCOVERABILITY_MISS.

Over time the acceptable irreducible model-bound share should concentrate in:

genuine novelty;

irreducible judgment;

real ambiguity;

high-value causal/architecture reasoning.

Everything else creates technical pressure toward machinery.

The model should progressively leave the deterministic control loop.

Target architecture:

software performs known workflow;

a semantic novelty/ambiguity/proof/reality fault occurs;

minimal relevant state is compiled;

appropriate model is invoked;

model resolves the irreducible uncertainty;

semantic delta is persisted;

deterministic execution resumes.

No model call should exist simply to say:

the test passed;

the build is still running;

now execute the next known command.

As reconstruction families mature, explicitly graduate them into zero-model regions.

Possible examples after evidence:

known SDK routines;

exact donors;

known thunks;

known stubs;

known wrappers;

known compiler idioms;

known map modules;

known geometry families;

known proof flows.

Once graduated:

frontier models are prohibited by default.

A contradiction or guard failure can deopt to general reasoning.

Whenever CPP controls or sufficiently knows the forward generator, evaluate using it to precompile the inverse.

Potential cases:

source → MWCC/PPC;

KME semantic map → rendered image;

UI structure → rendered screen;

state machine → behavior trace.

Generate controlled evidence where useful.

Prefer:

rules;

retrieval;

fingerprints;

constraint solving;

program synthesis;

specialized classifiers

before expensive generic model reasoning.

Synthetic evidence must never become self-confirming proof.

Maintain independent real-reference validation.

Do not prove an inverse reconstruction solely by feeding it through the same faulty assumptions that generated its training evidence.

Require independent evidence for production claims.

Synthetic round-trip is useful for:

training;

search;

benchmarking;

regression.

It is not automatically independent Production Reality.

Track oracle independence.

KME must become a proving ground for extreme visual reconstruction time compression.

Target the smallest generative semantic map representation.

Do not treat map reconstruction as pixel-to-block brute force.

Investigate:

camera recovery;

global scale/gauge;

topology;

symmetry;

semantic module recognition;

known asset retrieval;

palette/material family;

geometry parameters;

navigation/collision;

hidden geometry uncertainty;

render-back differential;

hidden-view prediction;

residual clustering;

incremental semantic patches;

proof invalidation.

Known map content should progressively become parsing/compilation.

Novel residual receives reasoning.

If current KME architecture permits:

generate synthetic semantic maps;

render controlled multiview references;

retain exact ground truth;

create hard-negative/contrastive variants;

benchmark inverse reconstruction;

learn minimum reference sets;

learn next-best-view strategies;

measure hidden-view generalization.

Separate:

curriculum;

development benchmark;

sealed holdout;

real-reference validation.

Do not claim visual reconstruction improvement from training examples alone.

Where evidence supports it, build/extend reusable institutional knowledge around:

Wii platform;

PPC/ABI;

compiler/toolchain behavior;

Nintendo SDK/runtime;

libraries;

shared engines;

types;

object models;

function families;

assets;

GX/rendering;

input;

audio;

filesystem/save;

runtime contracts;

emulator behavior;

hardware behavior;

cross-title homology.

Scope every fact correctly.

KSR-local knowledge must not become Wii-universal without evidence.

Before reasoning about a new Wii function/title:

test what is already known from:

same title versions;

WSR;

Wii Sports;

shared libraries;

shared SDK/runtime;

other legitimate comparable corpora.

Use whole-population matching where efficient.

Do not repeat per-function searches if corpus-level matching can establish reuse first.

Unknowns must become explicit enough that GSD X can reason about their dependencies.

An uncertainty should expose, where useful:

question;

current alternatives;

supporting evidence;

contradictory evidence;

downstream dependents;

critical-path relevance;

available discriminators;

expected resolution cost;

expected unlock;

proof requirement.

Do not require full probabilistic machinery everywhere.

Use structure where it changes decisions.

Search for unknowns through which many valid proof/closure paths pass.

Examples may include:

toolchain identity;

type layout;

state dispatcher;

camera gauge;

scale;

topology;

family identity.

Solving an uncertainty dominator can trigger a closure avalanche.

Prioritize it over low-leverage leaves where economics justify.

Every high-leverage proven fact should propagate through the current dependency/evidence graph.

A new:

type;

family;

toolchain fact;

homology;

camera model;

map module;

runtime contract

may change hundreds/thousands of candidate states.

After a new rule/fact:

re-drain affected unresolved population.

Continue cheap propagation to fixed point or economic bound.

Do not wait for agents to rediscover applicability.

Use the cheapest trustworthy oracle capable of resolving the claim.

Conceptually:

static;

compiler;

simulation/twin;

Dolphin/emulator;

remote runtime;

real Wii/hardware;

human sensory/product judgment.

Do not use expensive reality where cheap reality is sufficient.

Do not use cheap reality to overclaim a stronger boundary.

Apply/extend Cognitive Virtual Memory aggressively.

The institution is stateful.

The model is stateless.

Model context is a compiled working-set cache.

Not the authority.

Context must be a view of current live dependencies, not historical conversation.

Maintain:

small trusted kernel;

current Work Unit;

current uncertainty;

required evidence;

applicable capabilities;

proof contract.

Everything else is pageable/durable/cold as appropriate.

After semantic milestones such as:

decision sealed;

proof receipt created;

commit sealed;

hypothesis falsified;

Work Unit closed;

agent result consumed;

raw output compiled;

evict unnecessary context.

Do not wait for a giant emergency context wall.

A fresh worker should not need the previous transcript.

It receives:

Goal;

current semantic frontier;

relevant facts;

decisions;

proof;

uncertainty;

side effects;

invalidations;

capabilities;

budget;

next obligation.

If a fresh worker requires conversation archaeology:

institutional state is incomplete.

Avoid a giant parent model that reads every child result and schedules every next action.

Where dependencies are deterministic:

worker produces semantic receipt;

state updates;

scheduler identifies newly READY work;

next worker runs.

Parent cognition appears only for:

conflict;

novelty;

architecture;

ambiguous evidence;

Owner authority.

AGENT TEAMS Mode is active.

But Agent Teams are not automatically good.

Spawn only when there is genuine independent uncertainty/work and resource headroom.

Before spawn determine:

what independent question it resolves;

who consumes the result;

whether deterministic tooling is cheaper;

whether another worker already owns equivalent work;

whether independent duplication is deliberate assurance;

whether mutation scopes are safe.

Use:

fusion when workers share most working set;

fission when one worker spans unrelated domains;

singleflight for duplicate derivations.

Agent count is not a KPI.

In mature classes, fewer agents can represent success.

Agents communicate through compact durable semantic artifacts where possible.

Return:

facts;

evidence;

proof;

decisions;

uncertainty;

invalidations;

artifacts;

next dependency.

Do not send internal prose/transcripts between agents unless necessary.

Where appropriate, derived knowledge should be addressable by semantic/dependency identity rather than prompt wording.

Cache:

fact;

decision;

proof;

compiler result;

experiment;

family applicability;

context projection.

Invalidate on real dependency change.

Do not use arbitrary TTL as sole freshness strategy for stable engineering facts.

Verification must behave increasingly like an incremental build system.

A semantic delta invalidates only affected proof closure.

Do not rerun giant suites merely because a worker/session is new.

Proof receipt should know:

claim;

inputs;

dependencies;

environment/toolchain;

result;

evidence;

freshness;

invalidation.

Allow family/platform/toolchain proofs to be inherited by instances where applicable.

Instance proof can focus on:

membership;

parameters;

local residual;

changed behavior.

Proof cost should increasingly track novelty/blast radius.

Not population size.

Do not generate unbounded candidates faster than:

compile;

oracle;

proof;

hardware

can validate them.

Verification/oracle throughput is truth-production capacity.

Bound speculative queues.

Maintain headroom for critical-path experiments.

Do not saturate every resource merely to display activity.

Where reality permits, separate:

model cognition;

compiler CPU;

static analysis;

Dolphin runtime;

hardware;

proof;

storage/indexing.

A blocked runtime lane must not necessarily stall independent static/compile/research work.

Repeated patterns such as:

similar prompts;

similar diagnoses;

same mismatch;

same tool sequence;

same repair;

same proof;

same query

should generate an automation candidate.

Then:

shadow implementation;

historical replay;

benchmark;

negative control;

canary;

promotion if better.

This is the same Autonomous Optimization system operating inside Reconstruction Factory.

Do not build a separate miner if the universal optimizer can consume Reconstruction telemetry.

Version major proven factory capability states through existing governance.

Generation should represent actual verified capability.

Not marketing.

For each generation compare:

correctness;

cost;

wall-clock;

frontier attention;

deterministic coverage;

proof reuse;

family reuse;

false seals;

human intervention;

transfer.

A newer generation may lose.

Reality selects.

Every new reconstruction campaign should begin at the highest applicable institutional maturity.

Use the existing CBR / Project Birth concepts.

For every candidate inherited capability:

evaluate explicitly.

Do not allow silent omission.

Disposition must use existing canonical vocabulary if available.

Semantically distinguish:

inherit;

adapt;

already satisfied;

not applicable;

conflict;

unknown;

product-specific proposal.

Every campaign must periodically and finally return institutional capital.

Not a narrative summary.

Capture:

new capability;

improved capability;

new failure immunity;

negative-transfer boundary;

benchmark evidence;

new family;

new oracle;

new proof pattern;

new reusable tool;

new strategy;

capability discovered to be unnecessary;

capability ready for retirement.

Feed through existing UCR-CIF / Construction Return / Capability Runtime / CBR owners.

RATCHET A — RECONSTRUCTION CAPABILITY RATCHET

Each campaign may increase:

determinism;

reuse;

compiler understanding;

runtime understanding;

family coverage;

proof strength;

autonomy;

cost efficiency.

A later applicable campaign must not silently start below demonstrated maturity.

RATCHET B — INSTITUTIONAL ENGINEERING RATCHET

Reconstruction-derived patterns may promote, with evidence, from:

local;

family;

archetype;

domain;

cross-domain;

universal.

Then sibling systems inherit when applicable.

Inheritance does not end at project birth.

Compare current factory against current institutional frontier periodically or when a relevant capability is promoted.

If a better proven capability appears during a campaign:

evaluate migration economics.

Possible disposition:

immediate;

ratchet-on-touch;

next epoch;

next campaign;

optional;

do not migrate.

Do not keep a long campaign artificially old.

Every GSD X failure encountered by Reconstruction Factory is an institutional learning opportunity.

Examples:

lost state;

stale mission;

dead-but-green worker;

bad scheduling;

context explosion;

duplicate work;

unbounded retry;

poor handoff;

false done;

knowledge unreachable;

proof stale;

capability registered but inert.

Repair the immediate issue.

Then distill universal causal pattern.

Improve GSD X where justified.

Reconstruction Factory consumes GSD X and simultaneously certifies GSD X.

Production Reality Gate is mandatory at every material done boundary.

Testing commands are not production reality.

Registered capability is not active capability.

ACTIVE does not imply reachable.

REACHABLE does not imply effective.

EFFECTIVE does not imply PRODUCTION-PROVEN.

Demonstrate actual consumer/effect paths.

For reconstruction distinguish as applicable:

static proof;

build proof;

compiler/diff proof;

Dolphin/emulator proof;

remote runtime proof;

real hardware proof;

player/user reality;

human experience authority.

Do not overclaim.

Kernel vMAX-NULL-ERROR is active.

No done-gate may pass with known:

empty controls;

placeholder paths;

401s;

dead UI;

frontend/CLI disconnect;

registered-but-inert capability;

producer with no consumer;

consumer with no producer;

silent fallback changing semantics;

missing proof;

stale evidence treated as fresh;

benchmark with empty population;

mutation that did not mutate;

scanner that did not scan intended population;

cache without validity identity;

hidden cross-project leakage;

fake savings;

unmeasured claimed speedup;

unhandled error;

missing external authority falsely treated as PASS.

UNKNOWN is not PASS.

BLOCKED is not PASS.

STALE is not CURRENT.

MISSING is not NEGATIVE.

Every bug or failure discovered:

from this prompt;

from KME-L;

from current historical architecture;

during implementation;

during validation;

during benchmark;

during self-hosting;

during red-team

must be documented.

Concrete incident:

appropriate Knowledge Vault owner.

